# Session log — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Per-session record. Reverse-chronological — newest at top. Each entry captures what was attempted, what landed, and what's next.

## Format

```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD — <short title>

<one-paragraph summary of the session — what was the goal, what got done, what was learned>

**Changed:** <list of files or areas touched>
**Next:** <followups for the next session>

### (Optional) Audit — <scope> — YYYY-MM-DD

<audit-helper report body — appended by the `/audit` slash command>
```

Sessions can also contain `### Review`, `### Decision`, or other subheaders for in-session events worth recording separately.

## Conventions

- One H2 per session. If a single date has multiple sessions, suffix the title (`— morning`, `— deploy`, etc.).
- Keep summaries short — the diff and the commit messages are the canonical record of *what changed*. This log captures *why* and *what's next*.
- Don't delete old entries. They're the project's memory; the manager reads them when the work feels disoriented.
- `/audit` appends subheaders under the current day's entry — if no entry exists for today, create the stub first.

